\subsection{Sensitivity to flight power and booking resolution}
Uniformly increasing flight-phase power while retaining the original plans exposes their available energy margins. The numbers of feasible reference plans are 33, 26 and fifteen out of 36 under increases of 2\%, 5\% and 10\%, respectively. These are sensitivity scenarios applied to both service and positioning flights. At 5\%, 27 of the 36 greedy plans, 27 of the 36 local plans, twenty of the 28 originally admissible DeepSeek plans and 27 of the 36 Luna plans remain feasible. Differences in these counts also reflect the missions each plan serves.

Reoptimization at 5\% preserves full service in three representative tasks, selected by the first identifier at each scale with a violation in any originally feasible candidate. S01-B retains its original reference decisions. M01-B and L01-B each use one additional charging block in the new optimum, with no change of service routes. Their preferred weighted tardiness rises from 180 to 230 and from twelve to 83 minutes, respectively. Energy uncertainty can therefore change the charging schedule and its downstream delays even when all missions remain recoverable.

For L04-A, refining corridor and charger reservations from one minute to half a minute preserves the reference vector and the rejection of DeepSeek's answer. Its disjoint charging intervals both intersect $[52.5,53)$, so finer reservations at this resolution do not remove the conflict. Pad throughput and the departure grid remain one minute.
